WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:08.272
The Caterpillar had said that one side of the mushroom would make Alice grow.

2
00:00:08.273 --> 00:00:11.122
The other side would make her shrink.

3
00:00:11.123 --> 00:00:17.863
Then he'd disappeared before Alice could ask any questions.

4
00:00:17.864 --> 00:00:24.649
Alice studied the mushroom.

5
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:27.818
"How am I supposed to know which side does which?

6
00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:33.597
The mushroom cap is round, so it doesn't have a left side or a right side."

7
00:00:33.598 --> 00:00:36.761
There was only one way to find out.

8
00:00:36.762 --> 00:00:43.667
Alice stretched her arms around the mushroom and broke off a piece with each hand.

9
00:00:43.668 --> 00:00:49.556
"But which piece makes me grow?" Alice looked from one hand to the other.

10
00:00:49.557 --> 00:00:56.311
She finally decided to try the piece in her right hand.

11
00:00:56.312 --> 00:01:03.137
The next moment her chin hit something hard.

12
00:01:03.138 --> 00:01:05.200
It was her foot!

13
00:01:05.201 --> 00:01:12.982
Alice was frightened, but she managed to try the mushroom piece in her left hand.

14
00:01:12.983 --> 00:01:20.305
"That's better!" Alice said as her head started to rise.

15
00:01:20.306 --> 00:01:26.123
But her delight changed to panic when she couldn't see her shoulders.

16
00:01:26.124 --> 00:01:32.877
When she looked down, all she saw were her long neck and some green leaves.

17
00:01:32.878 --> 00:01:37.697
She didn't realize those were the tops of trees.

18
00:01:37.698 --> 00:01:41.347
"Where have my hands gone?" Alice asked.

19
00:01:41.348 --> 00:01:47.259
She couldn't see them below the leaves, so she bent her neck.

20
00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:50.170
"My neck is so flexible!

21
00:01:50.171 --> 00:01:52.567
It's almost like being a serpent.

22
00:01:52.568 --> 00:02:01.057
Oh!" Alice exclaimed in surprise as a bird flew at her face.

23
00:02:01.058 --> 00:02:05.181
"Serpent!" the Pigeon screamed.

24
00:02:05.182 --> 00:02:10.445
"I'm not a serpent!" Alice said angrily. "Leave me alone!"

25
00:02:10.446 --> 00:02:15.929
"No matter where I make my nest, serpents bother me!"

26
00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.993
The Pigeon sounded angry.

27
00:02:18.994 --> 00:02:23.571
"Night and day I must be on the lookout for serpents.

28
00:02:23.572 --> 00:02:27.019
I haven't slept in three weeks!"

29
00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:32.828
"I'm very sorry that you've been annoyed by serpents," Alice began. "But—"

30
00:02:32.829 --> 00:02:40.091
"I made my nest in the tallest tree, thinking I'd be free of the serpents," the Pigeon said.

31
00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:47.382
"But then you came wiggling down from the sky! Go away, Serpent!"

32
00:02:47.383 --> 00:02:51.176
"I'm not a serpent," Alice said.

33
00:02:51.177 --> 00:02:54.756
"I'm a . . . I mean, I'm a . . ."

34
00:02:54.757 --> 00:02:59.831
"Well! What are you?" the Pigeon demanded.

35
00:02:59.832 --> 00:03:03.772
"What are you trying to say?"

36
00:03:03.773 --> 00:03:09.189
"I . . . I'm a little girl," Alice finally said.

37
00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:15.758
She'd undergone so many changes, she wasn't sure what she was anymore.

38
00:03:15.759 --> 00:03:22.592
"I've seen lots of little girls but never one with such a long neck."

39
00:03:22.593 --> 00:03:25.864
The Pigeon looked at her skeptically.

40
00:03:25.865 --> 00:03:30.861
"No, you're a serpent, and you can't deny it.

41
00:03:30.862 --> 00:03:38.231
Next you'll be telling me that you've never eaten an egg."

42
00:03:38.232 --> 00:03:44.492
"I have eaten an egg," Alice admitted for she was a truthful child.

43
00:03:44.493 --> 00:03:47.816
"Little girls eat eggs as often as serpents do."

44
00:03:47.817 --> 00:03:51.926
"I don't believe that," the Pigeon said firmly.

45
00:03:51.927 --> 00:03:59.374
"And whether you're a girl or a serpent, you're looking for eggs."

46
00:03:59.375 --> 00:04:01.695
"I'm not looking for eggs.

47
00:04:01.696 --> 00:04:06.633
But if I were looking for them, I wouldn't want yours."

48
00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:11.206
Alice stamped her foot, and the ground shook.

49
00:04:11.207 --> 00:04:14.136
"I don't like raw eggs!"

50
00:04:14.137 --> 00:04:25.036
"Then go away!" The Pigeon still sounded angry as she settled into her nest again.

51
00:04:25.037 --> 00:04:32.645
Alice tried to crouch among the trees, but her neck kept getting tangled in branches.

52
00:04:32.646 --> 00:04:45.310
"I need to get back to my original size," she said to herself.

53
00:04:45.311 --> 00:04:56.085
Slowly and carefully, Alice nibbled from one piece of mushroom and then the other.

54
00:04:56.086 --> 00:05:00.198
At last, she was the correct size.

55
00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:08.274
"That's much better!" Alice said as she began to walk through the woods.

56
00:05:08.275 --> 00:05:14.445
Suddenly she came upon a space surrounding a house about four feet high.

57
00:05:14.446 --> 00:05:18.030
"I don't know who lives there," Alice said.

58
00:05:18.031 --> 00:05:23.775
"But they're sure to be smaller than I am, and I'll frighten them at this size."

59
00:05:23.776 --> 00:05:35.300
So Alice ate some more from the mushroom until she was only nine inches high.

